/users/W4RH4WK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-02-25T22:02:04Z","updated_at":"2021-02-25T22:02:04Z","body":"Here's a link to a related discussion on Amethyst: https://github.com/amethyst/amethyst/issues/2083","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/786257435/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"W4RH4WK","id":328798,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODc5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/328798?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK","html_url":"https://github.com/W4RH4WK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/W4RH4WK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808918326","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501#issuecomment-808918326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501","id":808918326,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgwODkxODMyNg==","user":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-28T16:13:02Z","updated_at":"2021-03-28T16:13:02Z","body":"Hi there!\r\n\r\nI'm working on the Amethyst issue on the same topic (see https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501#issuecomment-786257435). Although analysis is not yet 100% complete, there is the conclusion is that there is a minimum amount of strategies that provide a different balance of pro/cons (in short: CPU occupation <> precision).\r\n\r\nI think this is an issue that a game engine should definitely address. Based on a brief check, Bevy currently uses a simple [`thread::sleep()`](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/94c41840680afd414acb1195889bb88588901100/crates/bevy_app/src/schedule_runner.rs#L103).\r\n\r\nIs there any interest from the maintainers in addressing this problem? I can look into it. It needs to be thought though, how to expose this to the developer. For example, would an additional optional field in `RunMode::Loop` work? If so, which should be the default? Which should be the semantic? Should it describe the implementation (e.g. Sleep, Yield), or indicate where on the spectrum of precision it resides (Fast, Precise)?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808918326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808921158","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501#issuecomment-808921158","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501","id":808921158,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgwODkyMTE1OA==","user":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-28T16:32:52Z","updated_at":"2021-03-28T16:32:52Z","body":"So, I've actually missed YohDeadfall's comment above when posting here (as a consequence, ignore the proposal to implement different strategy).\r\n\r\nIn the current state, Bevy's logic is (as far as I understand) a standard loop with sleep (RunLoop), which is not different from Amethyst. \r\n\r\nThe current issue could be mitigated with the canonical `timeBeginPeriod`. In the longer term, the described event scheduler is an ideal solutiom, but in the meanwhile, `timeBeginPeriod` should be a simple enough intermediate step.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808921158/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808922100","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501#issuecomment-808922100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/1501","id":808922100,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDgwODkyMjEwMA==","user":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-28T16:40:32Z","updated_at":"2021-03-28T16:40:32Z","body":"> Usually this problem is fixed by an internal dispatcher provided by a framework and it should be there too (just started here, so has no idea on internals). The dispatcher works in a loop checking for messages from the operating system and running updates, but at the start of each cycle when system event handling is done it verifies user mode timers which are stored in a sorted list as tuples of a time to trigger and a handler. This method doesn't cause high CPU usage and provides more precise scheduling.\r\n\r\nThis is an interesting design. Can you provide some references to implementations (or even just theory)? I wonder what's the technical implementation, that is, how much it is an event listener, and how much a loop in a strict sense.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/808922100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"64kramsystem","id":1595356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTUzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1595356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem","html_url":"https://github.com/64kramsystem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/64kramsystem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u